#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:3
#: 6bfb79e2c2c14ed8bffbe19e806b328e
msgid "How to make any file persistent (bind-dirs)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:7
#: ab350c8a4efe483d942fbec13e817d93
msgid "This page is intended for advanced users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:10
#: 0c2a23a2843a4c44897a32f18094b523
msgid "What are bind-dirs?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:13
#: 8a5394599c48442caa10d55e09a5a6b1
msgid ""
"With `bind-dirs <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-core-agent-linux/blob/"
"master/vm-systemd/bind-dirs.sh>`__ any arbitrary files or folders can be "
"made persistent in app qubes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:16
#: 881b393c8d314be68bc1b5bbfd3790f6
msgid "What is it useful for?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:19
#: b043d31cbdd94daca76a099fb0decccb
msgid ""
"In an app qube all of the file system comes from the template except ``/"
"home``, ``/usr/local``, and ``/rw``. This means that changes in the rest of "
"the filesystem are lost when the app qube is shutdown. bind-dirs provides a "
"mechanism whereby files usually taken from the template can be persisted "
"across reboots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:21
#: cc4f679f88d64533a6447d9ba609b6ce
msgid ""
"For example, in Whonix, Tor’s data dir ``/var/lib/tor`` `has been made "
"persistent in the TemplateBased ProxyVM sys-whonix <https://github.com/"
"Whonix/qubes-whonix/blob/8438d13d75822e9ea800b9eb6024063f476636ff/usr/lib/"
"qubes-bind-dirs.d/40_qubes-whonix.conf#L5>`__. In this way sys-whonix can "
"benefit from the Tor anonymity feature ‘persistent Tor entry guards’ but "
"does not have to be a standalone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:24
#: 0bd2af071d4a4d8698395845a08ec2b8
msgid "How to use bind-dirs.sh?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:27
#: a6b2b744913b40359182ee6e194405bc
msgid ""
"In this example, we want to make ``/var/lib/tor`` persistent. Enter all of "
"the following commands in your app qube."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:29
#: df85d128bbd04fb89182e45880c9018d
msgid "Make sure the directory ``/rw/config/qubes-bind-dirs.d`` exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:37
#: 664e4dcea91b41e19c52c8fa26c6eaa6
msgid ""
"Create the file ``/rw/config/qubes-bind-dirs.d/50_user.conf`` with root "
"permissions, if it doesn’t already exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:45
#: 2b6a6805bf85428fb1960b9bb583ee3b
msgid ""
"Add a line to ``/rw/config/qubes-bind-dirs.d/50_user.conf`` that appends a "
"folder or file to the ``binds`` variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:53
#: d66a1607b8f94421948686013f9e38e8
msgid "Save."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:55
#: fefaf4cf8b794a8186c684d386cb1db1
msgid ""
"If the directory you wish to make persistent doesn’t exist in the template "
"on which the app qube is based, you’ll need to create the directory (with "
"its full path) under ``/rw/bind-dirs`` in the app qube. For example, if ``/"
"var/lib/tor`` didn’t exist in the template, then you would execute the "
"following command in your app qube:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:63
#: cadc7aa80cf248b5bb8e4936305f0cdf
msgid ""
"(optional) If the directory you want to persist across reboots (``/var/lib/"
"tor`` in this case) needs special ownership and permissions, make sure the "
"directory you created just under ``/rw/bind-dirs/`` has the same ones (using "
"the commands ``chown`` and ``chmod``, respectively)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:65
#: 13133f92af6e47038b58ea503e01901e
msgid "Reboot the app qube."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:67
#: 62146891aa044c0388c3c17720910d7d
msgid "Done."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:71
#: 620b1a0ad59f439ebbf3eb35d4fc2620
msgid ""
"From now on, all files in the ``/var/lib/tor`` directory will persist across "
"reboots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:73
#: a6b62b86a1984c60abe7d0846c42dcf9
msgid ""
"You can make as many files or folders persist as you want simply by making "
"multiple entries in the ``50_user.conf`` file, each on a separate line. For "
"example, if you added the file ``/etc/tor/torrc`` to the ``binds`` variable, "
"any modifications to *that* file would also persist across reboots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:83
#: 952bd7bf2d5f4e5b8b11c4956f9fcef5
msgid "Other Configuration Folders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:86
#: 90b368ed77b9451887d3c4970961e7c9
msgid "``/usr/lib/qubes-bind-dirs.d`` (lowest priority, for packages)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:88
#: d58c1b1775ed4fd8b9145170ad8dc38b
msgid ""
"``/etc/qubes-bind-dirs.d`` (intermediate priority, for template wide "
"configuration)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:90
#: ae4f211c2da64e19983fb4e542d75faa
msgid ""
"``/rw/config/qubes-bind-dirs.d`` (highest priority, for per VM configuration)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:95
#: 5f39a7a3473e44aa83df122aaf5b2bcc
msgid "How does it work?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:98
#: cb83de97a55e4688ae99f4c2fb74fc34
msgid ""
"bind-dirs.sh is called at startup of an app qube, and configuration files in "
"the above configuration folders are parsed to build a bash array. Files or "
"folders identified in the array are copied to ``/rw/bind-dirs`` if they do "
"not already exist there, and are then bind mounted over the original files/"
"folders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:100
#: e01e067aec6741bba5f6a2553b94d6aa
msgid ""
"Creation of the files and folders in ``/rw/bind-dirs`` should be automatic "
"the first time the app qube is restarted after configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:102
#: 550185097f584c6f8b2142b287e1bb36
msgid ""
"If you want to circumvent this process, you can create the relevant file "
"structure under ``/rw/bind-dirs`` and make any changes at the same time that "
"you perform the configuration, before reboot. Note that you must create the "
"full folder structure under ``/rw/bind-dirs`` - e.g you would have to create "
"``/rw/bind-dirs/var/lib/tor``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:105
#: 8d369a3a054d4094acbf185baf8a9e68
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:108
#: 94055bd8cd924cc88e3128d2bfc91a91
msgid ""
"Files that exist in the template root image cannot be deleted in the app "
"qubes root image using bind-dirs.sh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:110
#: 6e40de99b6634949ba1304ac08000019
msgid ""
"Re-running ``sudo /usr/lib/qubes/init/bind-dirs.sh`` without a previous "
"``sudo /usr/lib/qubes/init/bind-dirs.sh umount`` does not work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:112
#: 09471d9dbd7a4f3a90406f485608fea0
msgid ""
"Running ``sudo /usr/lib/qubes/init/bind-dirs.sh umount`` after boot (before "
"shutdown) is probably not sane and nothing can be done about that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:114
#: 2a9ecfa9c1f5408c91a2e927c098bbb5
msgid ""
"Many editors create a temporary file and copy it over the original file. If "
"you have bind mounted an individual file this will break the mount. Any "
"changes you make will not survive a reboot. If you think it likely you will "
"want to edit a file, then either include the parent directory in bind-dirs "
"rather than the file, or perform the file operation on the file in ``/rw/"
"bind-dirs``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:116
#: 6bd765e0f6af47d5ae83906bb8375195
msgid ""
"Some files are altered when a qube boots - e.g. ``/etc/hosts``. If you try "
"to use bind-dirs on such files you may break your qube in unpredictable "
"ways. You can add persistent rules to ``/etc/hosts`` using :doc:`/rw/config/"
"rc.local </user/advanced-topics/config-files>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:121
#: 20233107435f4a22b92a839fe08f9a93
msgid "How to remove binds from bind-dirs.sh?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:124
#: f2288da1b27648d6b258b03bff8ec4d7
msgid ""
"``binds`` is actually just a bash variable (an array) and the bind-dirs.sh "
"configuration folders are sourced as bash snippets in lexical order. "
"Therefore if you wanted to remove an existing entry from the ``binds`` "
"array, you could do that by using a lexically higher configuration file. For "
"example, if you wanted to make ``/var/lib/tor`` non-persistent in ``sys-"
"whonix`` without manually editing ``/usr/lib/qubes-bind-dirs.d/40_qubes-"
"whonix.conf``, you could use the following in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:126
#: c28f9ac5de494d01b21ccc9440855979
msgid "``/rw/config/qubes-bind-dirs.d/50_user.conf``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:134
#: 6b02d65a2c144b6e87deee57045b2a01
msgid ""
"(Editing ``/usr/lib/qubes-bind-dirs.d/40_qubes-whonix.conf`` directly is "
"strongly discouraged, since such changes get lost when that file is changed "
"in the package on upgrades.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:137
#: 59da149394e349f3a8afaef5cf3eeae8
msgid "Custom persist feature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:140
#: 0fd7b56f78e94215b66d387578231dfd
msgid ""
"Custom persist is an optional advanced feature allowing the creation of "
"minimal state AppVM. The purpose of such an AppVM is to avoid unwanted data "
"to persist as much as possible by disabling the ability to configure "
"persistence from the VM itself. When enabled, the following happens:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:142
#: 746085c647214339bc5d6a40c6a6de9a
msgid "``/rw/config/rc.local`` is no longer executed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:144
#: 2dfd088857c6413b898fb4c5a16d2424
msgid "``/rw/config/qubes-firewall-user-script`` is ignored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:146
#: faaabf65d4794ff89086e72e22747812
msgid "``/rw/config/suspend-module-blacklist`` is ignored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:148
#: ac67dff35758461eaa7bc27233be5f73
msgid ""
"User bind dirs defined in ``/rw/config/qubes-bind-dirs.d`` are no longer read"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:150
#: 21ea1b408d0241fb84a41ca4c12440fc
msgid ""
"``/home`` and ``/user/local`` are not persistent anymore unless explicitly "
"configured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:154
#: de96c0272ab946f9ba7c9e14ea5e941f
msgid ""
"Bind dirs are obviously still supported but this must be configured either "
"in the template (``/usr/lib/qubes-bind-dirs.d`` and ``/etc/qubes-bind-dirs."
"d``) or from dom0 using ``qvm-features``. The bind dirs declaration must be "
"done this way: ``qvm-features <VMNAME> custom-persist.<ARBITRARY NAME> [PRE-"
"CREATION SETTINGS]<PATH>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:156
#: 616a2549331d47ef99c638700343e790
msgid "To use this feature, first, enable it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:164
#: 179030005dc941daa55bbde22726dd97
msgid "Then, configure a persistent directory with ``qvm-features``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:172
#: a63f58e9ea5647ffb8c350fd37414304
msgid ""
"To re-enable ``/home`` and ``/usr/local`` persistence, just add them to the "
"list:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:181
#: 1ae12b7be1a842eea8dce58a441aea72
msgid ""
"When starting the VM, declared custom-persist bind dirs are automatically "
"added to the ``binds`` variable described above and are handled in the same "
"way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/bind-dirs.rst:183
#: abfd40184c5e424e890ba7e7fca8aa6c
msgid ""
